@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
 
 Exact native canary: quota16 versus100 took30939ms versus4833ms (6.4016x); quota336 supplied3.242x four-worker throughput. Tested image c1619eec and loader e4eeb994 were installed under versioned paths. Guest launch measurement62ac7aab was added to local admission and relay marketplace policy, preserving existing entries and administrator authority.
 
-Production activation: Node/Shield/Network wrappers restarted19:17–19:19UTC; control and storage VMs stayed running. Marketplace policy was corrected19:23. The node reconciled old VMs through its normal guarded recovery. All nine original apps were running on the new runtime19:31 with exact CPU quota and matching application-memory shares. TLS verification is separate and still underway; initial failures and recovery receipts are retained.
+Production activation: Node/Shield/Network wrappers restarted19:17–19:19UTC; control and storage VMs stayed running. Marketplace policy was corrected19:23. The node reconciled old VMs through its normal guarded recovery. All nine original apps were running on the new runtime19:31 with exact CPU quota and matching application-memory shares. At19:41UTC all nine passed CA/hostname-verified HTTPS and HTTP200 through all18 currently DNS-advertised addresses. Earlier TLS, DNS and cron readiness failures during recovery are retained as evidence; the final probe passed.
 
 Rollback: preserve the original installed runtime.bin and shield-host.exe and staging backups. Verify current candidate hashes, stop only the three exact scheduled tasks, confirm listeners closed, then run the rollback phase and rollback-start-shield/network/node in order. The original stop phase intentionally checks PRE-UPGRADE hashes and must not be reused to stop the new runtime. Do not force-remove tenant VMs: let the node reconcile them. The relay policy rollback is a separate compare-and-swap operation using its pre-change backup. Restoring old software restores its known CPU enforcement defect. Reverify all apps, leases, ingress certificates, and secret-dependent operation.
 
